      "archaeologicalRemains": "traces",
      "details": "<p><span>The gate\u2019s approximate location is based on an aerial photograph of Nineveh taken in 1929, Corona satellite imagery (1967-68), and Google satellite imagery. The location of the gate suggested here is\u00a0</span>the traditional spot of the\u00a0<a class=\"external-link\" href=\"../960751425\" target=\"_self\" title=\"A\u0161\u0161ur Gate\">A\u0161\u0161ur Gate</a>\u00a0according to most modern reconstructions of Nineveh. Those maps place the Halzi Gate about 400 m north of the southeast corner (approximate coordinates: 36.3398677, 43.1777291).</p>",
      "review_state": "published",
